    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but the resonance theory doesnt explain why it seems to react to the specific pressure shifts. like, every time the barometer drops, the rhythm of the pulses changes. it feels way too deliberate for just structural noise. if someone were using something like Very Low Frequency (VLF) or even ELF waves, which are known to penetrate through almost anything, wouldn't a certain atmospheric configuration make those signals way more prominent or even \"readable\" in the environment? i'm just wondering if there's a technical way someone could use these weather anomalies to hide a transmission stream.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
